## P18-V01 Push updateCorePoolSize Rust parity — 2026-10-16

- Code commit `8105fd3b` changes the public facade result from `bool` to `Result<(), PushConsumerError>` and preserves Java's void/no-op contract. It distinguishes an uncreated service (`NotStarted`), invalid live-facade bounds (no-op success), and a requested size above the constructed executor maximum after a live config increase (`InvalidSetting`, corresponding to Java `IllegalArgumentException`). Concurrent and orderly service owners now permit the executor maximum itself when the facade maximum has since been raised. The service maximum is retained across shutdown and startup failure, while accepted post-shutdown changes update the tracked effective size without restarting workers.
- Added fixture-backed Rust regression coverage for the missing-service path, valid/invalid values, concurrent and orderly resizing, live maximum increase, executor-capacity failure, exact-capacity acceptance, and shutdown behavior. Updated `tests/push_pipeline.rs` for the new Rust error result.
- PASS on the committed code: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-features --locked` (220 unit tests, all integration targets and 12 doctests); `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`; pinned `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` (37 scenarios, all fixture-drift checks and Rust/Java cross-decodes; exit 0).
- One verification wrapper initially returned exit 1 after Maven completed because zsh reserves the variable name `status`; reran with `mvn_result` and confirmed Maven verify exit 0. No Maven fixture or project failure occurred.
- Updated `docs/compatibility/PHASE_10_OFFLINE_METHOD_MATRIX.md` and `docs/release-checklist.md` in a separate documentation change. Broad P18-V01, full-workspace P18-V02 on this final revision, GitHub Ubuntu/P18-V04 evidence, and release preflight remain open. No plan file, live Broker/Docker environment, publication, push, or tag was changed.

